          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homeowners the first laser should be a compact self-leveling cross-line: red when money is tight and the rooms are dim, green when they are bright. That one tool handles shelves, art, televisions and trim faster than any spirit level, and the Bosch GLL55 and Klein 93LCLS are dependable options.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Step up to a three-plane green laser such as the Huepar 903CG, Bosch GLL3-330CG or DeWalt DW089LG for cabinets, tile, framing or ceilings, and to a rotary kit like the Johnson for outdoor grading. Whichever you choose, switch it off before moving it, mark the same part of the line every time, and run the two-wall check after any drop.
